    {
      "id": "u_0f4389bc294d341f535e2f49_0",
      "kind": "p",
      "source": "Now, I'm starting to learn about __TRILIUM_PH_0__Bash__TRILIUM_PH_1__ and would like to create notes related to this topic. But now I'm facing a problem of where to categorize this. The issue here is that Bash is both a programming language and a tool (shell) very much tied into Linux. It seems it belongs to both of these, I can't (and don't want to) choose one over the other.",
      "sourceHash": "0f4389bc294d341f535e2f4964e748cd8ffe47f8f1ace4b76d74467b4bdacc50",
      "context": "Cloning Notes > Motivation",
      "contextHash": "ef7a987b8b26daba7a4e897731622e58f856f900fbc386aabd785c21728ed4a7",
      "status": "pending",
      "active": true
    },
    {
      "id": "u_175b1c68d2ef626afa449c5d_0",
      "kind": "h2",
      "source": "Solution__TRILIUM_PH_0__",
      "sourceHash": "175b1c68d2ef626afa449c5d146fecd79bce81c9a43480b598750933d41b5033",
      "context": "Cloning Notes > Solution",
      "contextHash": "085aac6bed276747ea3413db1653dacef31ce717ff0aebb6e53b6b99ed8fec87",
      "status": "pending",
      "active": true
    },
    {
      "id": "u_bca57fd5510f068b72dcb6bf_0",
      "kind": "p",
      "source": "The solution to the problem shown above is to allow notes to have multiple parents.",
      "sourceHash": "bca57fd5510f068b72dcb6bf43397e05714a7d167226196a19ad820c8ca79b32",
      "context": "Cloning Notes > Solution",
      "contextHash": "085aac6bed276747ea3413db1653dacef31ce717ff0aebb6e53b6b99ed8fec87",
      "status": "pending",
      "active": true
    },
    {
      "id": "u_4aee0b7ce63b428e57f3e05d_0",
      "kind": "p",
      "source": "I call these \"clones\", but that is a bit misleading - there's no original and cloned note - the notes in both of the parents categories are identical.",
      "sourceHash": "4aee0b7ce63b428e57f3e05d705d523b86e8b646fff3dedeb7f706543a1e3509",
      "context": "Cloning Notes > Solution",
      "contextHash": "085aac6bed276747ea3413db1653dacef31ce717ff0aebb6e53b6b99ed8fec87",
      "status": "pending",
      "active": true
    },
    {
      "id": "u_7cc70cef75a74ac113140e1f_0",
      "kind": "p",
      "source": "Another misleading thing about \"cloning\" is that it suggests that a copy of the note has been made. That's not really true, the note itself stays in just one original, it is just referenced in multiple places in the tree hierarchy. So changing it in one category changes it in all the others, because they're all the same note.",
      "sourceHash": "7cc70cef75a74ac113140e1f7923c2eadc4ff52e9b6d767fd43a4b0bca537cfd",
      "context": "Cloning Notes > Solution",
      "contextHash": "085aac6bed276747ea3413db1653dacef31ce717ff0aebb6e53b6b99ed8fec87",
      "status": "pending",
      "active": true
    },
    {
      "id": "u_53ef88fcf612766c54733a9a_0",
      "kind": "p",
      "source": "Here's the final structure with cloning:",
      "sourceHash": "53ef88fcf612766c54733a9a295b4e264a2f3ad28a04e448720175d99b560da7",
      "context": "Cloning Notes > Solution",
      "contextHash": "085aac6bed276747ea3413db1653dacef31ce717ff0aebb6e53b6b99ed8fec87",
      "status": "pending",
      "active": true
